That last one has a visible price, and finding it explains a defect
the earlier eDP bring-up had already recorded without a cause.
bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_edp/trilinear_dp14/
trilinear_dp14.c:257-258 programs the AUX clock divider from

    // FIXME: 200 refer to raw code from SHC
    u32 src_apb_clk = 200;

200 is the AHB rate in MHz. The variable is even named src_apb_clk. The vendor
hardcoded the one number its own clock model could not have told it: ask its
"edp" gate for a rate and it answers 26 MHz. `drm-allwinner-a733-displayport-aux` computes that divider from
clk_get_rate() with a range check that refuses rather than guesses, which only
works because the bus gate is parented to something true.

AND THE HALF THAT USUALLY GETS SKIPPED: WHERE THE VENDOR IS RIGHT
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The same comparison also lists agreement, and here it is a substantial list. These were reached
from the UM and from the failure modes of the mainline primitives before the
vendor tree was opened; the agreement is a cross-check, not a source.

  - The four-way mux order (VIDEO0/1/2PLL4X, PERI0PLL2X) and both dividers
    linear. Its private CCU_FEATURE_MP_NO_INDEX_MODE (ccu_mp.c:140, ccu_mp.h:55)
    is mainline's CCU_FEATURE_DUAL_DIV under another name. Same conclusion the
    UM states outright.
  - CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT on edp-tv, and
    CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT on the 4X taps (ccu-sun60iw2.c:216, 1689-1697) -- the
    exact flag set this patch chose.
  - min_rate 1272000000. Not a rounding accident: it is the lowest VCO that is
    both inside Table 4-2's window and exactly reachable from 24 MHz, which is
    what makes ccu_nm_determine_rate()'s clamp agree with what
    ccu_nm_set_rate() can produce. Taken, with the reasoning written down.
  - clk_set_rate() on the TCON module clock as the modeset mechanism
    (bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/sunxi_tcon.c:81, :802), which is what makes
    propagation the right answer rather than a convenience.
  - DISPLAY1_TOP as its own device with its own clock, gate and reset
    (bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/sunxi_tcon_top.c:32-99, asking for
    "clk_bus_dpss_top", "rst_bus_dpss_top" and a clock it calls "clk_ahb") --
    the same shape mainline uses for sun8i-tcon-top, and the reason this patch
    adds DPSS_TOP1's ids without folding them into the TCON node.
  - And the arithmetic: VCO 1848 / P0 6 / M 2 for 1920x1200. We land on the
    same numbers from the UM formula. Two independent derivations agreeing is
    the strongest thing this patch has short of the board.

One near-miss worth recording so nobody else spends the time: its
sunxi_tcon_lcd_set_clk() DOES compare the rate it got against the rate it asked
for (sunxi_tcon.c:82-85) -- and then reports the mismatch at DRM_INFO and
carries on. It notices and does not act.

